  "body": "## What changed\n\nPart 2 of #3751: `camcraft-cli --skill <folder|claude|copilot> install [--dir <path>] [--user] [--force]`. The command writes an AI agent skill that teaches the CLI. Part 1 (`--ui`, PR #3861) does not change.\n\n- New lane `crates/app/src/cli_skill.rs`. It is a `HELP_LANES` entry, so the help tests check it. `cli.rs` gets the usage lines and one dispatch line, and stays under 400 lines (393).\n- One source for the skill text: the hand-written body `crates/app/src/cli_skill.md` (our own text), then a generated \"Command reference\". The reference is `TOP_USAGE` and each `HELP_LANES` usage text, exactly as the binary prints them. Thus a new lane or flag shows in the skill with no edit.\n- Targets:\n  - `folder`: `<dir>/SKILL.md` with the Agent Skills header (`name`, `description`). `--dir` is necessary.\n  - `claude`: `.claude/skills/camcraft-cli/SKILL.md` in the current folder (or `--dir`). With `--user`: `~/.claude/skills/camcraft-cli/SKILL.md` (`HOME`, else `USERPROFILE`).\n  - `copilot`: `.github/instructions/camcraft-cli.instructions.md` with `applyTo: \"**\"`, from the GitHub Copilot repository custom instructions documentation. The user's own `.github/copilot-instructions.md` is not touched.\n- The command never replaces a file silently. When the target file is there, it exits 1, names the path, writes nothing and names `--force`.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/3751-cli-skill-install.md` (target paths and their sources, the default scope, the overwrite rule, no MCP tool).\n\n## Pinning tests (`camcraft-app`, suite `cli`)\n\n- `skill_folder_target_writes_skill_md_into_the_given_folder`\n- `skill_claude_target_writes_the_project_skill_or_with_user_the_home_skill`\n- `skill_copilot_target_writes_an_instructions_file_for_all_paths`\n- `skill_install_never_replaces_a_file_without_force`\n- `skill_text_names_every_cli_lane_and_no_other` (the drift test: the skill names each lane in `HELP_LANES`, and each `camcraft-cli <word>` in the skill is a lane that exists)\n- The existing `every_subcommand_answers_help_and_names_its_flags` and `every_listed_command_is_a_help_lane` now walk the `--skill` lane too.\n\nEach target test runs the real binary in a temporary folder, with `HOME` and `USERPROFILE` set to a temporary folder.\n\n## Gate\n\nQuick gate on head `5f4316003`: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (with `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`, `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`): 10 steps, 0 failed.\n- `app build`, `app suites: lib`, `ai_guide`, `cli` (18 passed), `default_machine_missing`, `example_catalog`, `first_part_programs`, `mcp`, `mcp_verify`, `regression_models`: ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The light lane did not run: no light twin covers this change (no toolpath, post or geometry code).\n- Note: two earlier gate runs with sccache failed at the build step with `error[E0463]: can't find crate for camcraft_cl` (a bad cached rlib, not this diff). A `cargo clean -p` of our crates and a run without sccache fixed it.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No Claude Code or Copilot session read the installed files. The tests check the paths and the headers only.\n- Windows and macOS: not built. The code uses only `std::fs` and `std::env`.\n- No heavy lane and no light lane step: the change touches no toolpath, post or geometry code.\n\n## MCP\n\nNo MCP tool and no follow-up issue. The lane writes a text file for an agent. It changes no document state and has no undo, so it is not a command in the sense of \"Everything Is a Command\". An MCP agent already reads the tool table with `camcraft-cli mcp reference`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- New tests join the existing top-level `cli` suite (`crates/app/tests/cli.rs`, 386 lines). No new test binary.\n- No process file changes: the repository's own `.claude/skills/` is not touched.\n\nChangelog: `camcraft-cli --skill <folder|claude|copilot> install` writes an AI agent skill for the CLI (lanes, exit codes, examples and the full help text). It refuses to replace an existing file without `--force`.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nFixes #3751\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
